---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="electronics"
  title="RC, RL and RLC Circuits"
  description="Put a resistor with something that stores energy and the circuit stops answering instantly. A capacitor and a resistor give one time constant and a lazy approach to the answer; add an inductor and the two stores start passing energy back and forth, so the circuit rings, and how fast the ringing dies is a knob you can turn. The same two poles decide the transient, the ringing and which frequencies get through."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="rlc" width="1000" height="660"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn" id="run">Pause</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">Reset</button>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Circuit</label>
        <div class="seg" id="mode">
          <button data-m="rc" class="active">RC</button>
          <button data-m="rl">RL</button>
          <button data-m="rlc">RLC</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Side panel</label>
        <div class="seg" id="aux">
          <button data-a="energy" class="active">Energy</button>
          <button data-a="poles">Poles</button>
          <button data-a="bode">Bode</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Source</label>
        <div class="seg" id="src">
          <button data-s="step" class="active">Step</button>
          <button data-s="square">Square</button>
          <button data-s="sine">Sine</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Amplitude <b id="ampval">5.0 V</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="amp" min="5" max="120" step="1" value="50" />
      </div>

      <div class="control" id="ctl-f">
        <label>Drive frequency <b id="fval">—</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="freq" min="-170" max="70" step="1" value="-80" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>slow</span><span>far past resonance</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Resistance R <b id="rval">—</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="r" min="2" max="300" step="1" value="200" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>rings for ages</span><span>refuses to ring</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control" id="ctl-l">
        <label>Inductance L <b id="lval">—</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="l" min="1" max="200" step="1" value="50" />
      </div>

      <div class="control" id="ctl-c">
        <label>Capacitance C <b id="cval">—</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="c" min="1" max="200" step="1" value="20" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Time rate <b id="rateval">1.0×</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="rate" min="10" max="400" step="5" value="100" />
      </div>

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="row"><span id="l1">—</span><b id="r1">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l2">—</span><b id="r2">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l3">—</span><b id="r3">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l4">—</span><b id="r4">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l5">—</span><b id="r5">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l6">—</span><b id="r6">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l7">—</span><b id="r7">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l8">—</span><b id="r8">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-faint);margin:0;line-height:1.5">
        The poles panel is the same circuit seen from the Laplace side. Move R
        and watch the two poles travel; everything else on screen follows them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Start on <b>RC</b> with a step. The capacitor does not jump, because
      jumping would need infinite current through R. It fills at a rate set by
      how much is still missing, which is what makes the curve an exponential,
      and after one <b>τ = RC</b> it has covered 63% of the gap. That mark is
      drawn on the scope.
    </li>
    <li>
      Now <b>RL</b>. The roles swap: the current is what refuses to jump, and
      the inductor briefly puts the whole source voltage across itself to stop
      it. Same shape, same kind of τ = L/R, but the quantity that has inertia is
      the current rather than the charge.
    </li>
    <li>
      Switch to <b>RLC</b> and drop R low. Now there are two stores and they
      argue: the capacitor dumps into the inductor, the inductor refuses to stop
      and <b>overcharges the capacitor the other way</b>, and the whole thing
      rings. Watch the energy panel, where the two bars trade back and forth
      while the total slowly leaks away through R.
    </li>
    <li>
      Raise R and watch the ringing die sooner. Keep going and at
      <b>ζ = 1</b> it stops ringing at all: the fastest approach that never
      overshoots, which is why <b>critically damped</b> is what you want a door
      closer or a car suspension to be. Past that it is overdamped and just
      sluggish.
    </li>
    <li>
      Switch the side panel to <b>Poles</b> and do it again. Underdamped, they sit as a
      <b>complex pair</b>, their distance from the origin is ω₀ and their height
      is the frequency you can hear in the ringing. At ζ = 1 they collide on the
      real axis and then split apart along it. Every shape the scope draws is
      already written there.
    </li>
    <li>
      Switch the source to <b>Sine</b> and sweep the frequency. Slow, and the
      output follows the input; fast, and it cannot keep up. The <b>Bode</b>
      panel is that whole experiment done at once, and the point where it has
      fallen by 3 dB is the same <b>1/τ</b> the step response showed you. One
      circuit, one number, two apparently unrelated measurements.
    </li>
    <li>
      With RLC underdamped, put the drive right on <b>f₀</b>. The output climbs
      well past the input: at resonance the reactances cancel and only R is left
      to limit anything, so the capacitor voltage overshoots the source by
      roughly <b>Q</b>. Turn R down to make Q large and watch how long it takes
      the amplitude to build.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText, subHtml } from '../../../lib/sim';

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // One series loop, integrated in the two variables that carry the memory:
  // the capacitor's voltage and the inductor's current. Everything else on the
  // page is a different view of the same two numbers.
  //
  //     RC   C dv/dt = (vs - v)/R
  //     RL   L di/dt = vs - iR
  //     RLC  L di/dt = vs - iR - v ,  C dv/dt = i
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  type Mode = 'rc' | 'rl' | 'rlc';
  type Src = 'step' | 'square' | 'sine';

  const state = {
    mode: 'rc' as Mode,
    src: 'step' as Src,
    aux: 'energy' as 'energy' | 'poles' | 'bode',
    amp: 5, // V
    fmul: 0.15, // drive frequency, as a multiple of the circuit's own
    R: 100, // Ω
    L: 0.05, // H
    C: 2e-6, // F
    rate: 1,
    running: true,
  };

  let i = 0; // inductor / loop current, A
  let vC = 0; // capacitor voltage, V
  let clock = 0; // simulated seconds
  let eDiss = 0; // joules turned to heat since reset

  const hasL = () => state.mode !== 'rc';
  const hasC = () => state.mode !== 'rl';

  /** The circuit's own timescale, in Hz, whatever it is made of. */
  function fchar() {
    if (state.mode === 'rc') return 1 / (2 * Math.PI * state.R * state.C);
    if (state.mode === 'rl') return state.R / (2 * Math.PI * state.L);
    return 1 / (2 * Math.PI * Math.sqrt(state.L * state.C));
  }
  const w0 = () => 2 * Math.PI * fchar();
  /** Damping ratio. Only the RLC has a meaningful one. */
  const zeta = () => (state.R / 2) * Math.sqrt(state.C / state.L);
  const tauOf = () =>
    state.mode === 'rc' ? state.R * state.C : state.mode === 'rl' ? state.L / state.R : 1 / (zeta() * w0());
  const driveF = () => state.fmul * fchar();

  function vSource(t: number) {
    if (state.src === 'step') return t > 0 ? state.amp : 0;
    const ph = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * driveF() * t);
    if (state.src === 'sine') return state.amp * ph;
    return state.amp * (ph >= 0 ? 1 : 0); // square, from 0 to amp
  }

  // --- integration -----------------------------------------------------------

  function deriv(ii: number, vv: number, vs: number) {
    if (state.mode === 'rc') return { di: 0, dv: (vs - vv) / (state.R * state.C) };
    if (state.mode === 'rl') return { di: (vs - ii * state.R) / state.L, dv: 0 };
    return { di: (vs - ii * state.R - vv) / state.L, dv: ii / state.C };
  }

  function rk4(h: number, vs: number) {
    const a = deriv(i, vC, vs);
    const b = deriv(i + (h * a.di) / 2, vC + (h * a.dv) / 2, vs);
    const c = deriv(i + (h * b.di) / 2, vC + (h * b.dv) / 2, vs);
    const d = deriv(i + h * c.di, vC + h * c.dv, vs);
    i += (h / 6) * (a.di + 2 * b.di + 2 * c.di + d.di);
    vC += (h / 6) * (a.dv + 2 * b.dv + 2 * c.dv + d.dv);
    if (state.mode === 'rc') i = (vs - vC) / state.R;
  }

  type Sample = { t: number; vs: number; vC: number; vL: number; i: number };
  let hist: Sample[] = [];

  const spanOf = () =>
    state.src === 'sine'
      ? Math.max(6 / Math.max(driveF(), 1e-6), 4 * tauOf())
      : state.src === 'square'
        ? 2 / Math.max(driveF(), 1e-6)
        : 12 * tauOf();

  function physics(dtReal: number) {
    // A step is one experiment with an end, so let it finish and stay on screen
    // rather than scrolling the interesting part away.
    if (state.src === 'step' && clock > spanOf()) return;
    // Real seconds are far too long to watch a millisecond circuit in, so the
    // clock is slowed to fill the scope in about five seconds whatever the
    // components are. The numbers on screen are still the circuit's own.
    const dt = dtReal * state.rate * (spanOf() / 5);
    const scale = Math.min(tauOf(), 1 / Math.max(w0(), 1e-9));
    const steps = Math.max(24, Math.min(4000, Math.ceil(dt / (scale * 0.02))));
    const h = dt / steps;
    for (let s = 0; s < steps; s++) {
      const vs = vSource(clock);
      rk4(h, vs);
      clock += h;
      eDiss += i * i * state.R * h;
      if (s % Math.ceil(steps / 8) === 0) push(vs);
    }
    push(vSource(clock));
    const span = spanOf();
    if (state.src !== 'step')
      while (hist.length > 2 && hist[0].t < clock - span) hist.shift();
    if (hist.length > 6000) hist.splice(0, hist.length - 6000);
  }

  function push(vs: number) {
    const vL = hasL() ? vs - i * state.R - (hasC() ? vC : 0) : 0;
    hist.push({ t: clock, vs, vC, vL, i });
  }

  function reset() {
    i = 0;
    vC = 0;
    clock = 0;
    eDiss = 0;
    hist = [];
  }

  // --- canvas ----------------------------------------------------------------

  const canvas = document.getElementById('rlc') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const cssv = (n: string) => getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(n).trim();
  const inkA = (a: number) => `rgba(${cssv('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236'},${a})`;
  const bg = () => cssv('--stage-bg') || '#0d0e12';
  const { label } = makeText(ctx, inkA);

  const WARM = '#f59e0b'; // source voltage
  const TEAL = '#5eead4'; // capacitor
  const ACC = '#7c8cff'; // inductor
  const GREEN = '#34d399'; // current
  const HOT = '#f9736a';

  // The loop and the scope are always there; the third panel is one of
  // energy / poles / Bode, picked in the side panel.
  const CIRC = { x: 20, y: 74, w: 610, h: 300 };
  const AUX = { x: 660, y: 74, w: 320, h: 300 };
  const SCOPE = { x: 20, y: 418, w: 960, h: 220 };
  const ENERGY = AUX, POLES = AUX, BODE = AUX;

  function rr(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, r: number) {
    const rad = Math.min(r, Math.abs(w) / 2, Math.abs(h) / 2);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x + rad, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w - rad, y);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y, x + w, y + rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w, y + h - rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y + h, x + w - rad, y + h);
    ctx.lineTo(x + rad, y + h);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y + h, x, y + h - rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x, y + rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y, x + rad, y);
    ctx.closePath();
  }
  function panel(p: { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number }, title: string) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.1);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    rr(p.x, p.y, p.w, p.h, 10);
    ctx.stroke();
    label(title, p.x + 2, p.y - 9, 0.5, 'left', 11);
  }

  function eng(v: number, unit: string, digits = 2): string {
    const a = Math.abs(v);
    if (a === 0) return `0 ${unit}`;
    const steps: [number, string][] = [
      [1e-15, 'f'], [1e-12, 'p'], [1e-9, 'n'], [1e-6, 'µ'], [1e-3, 'm'],
      [1, ''], [1e3, 'k'], [1e6, 'M'], [1e9, 'G'],
    ];
    let pick = steps[0];
    for (const s of steps) if (a >= s[0]) pick = s;
    return `${(v / pick[0]).toFixed(digits)} ${pick[1]}${unit}`;
  }

  // --- the circuit -----------------------------------------------------------

  const LX = CIRC.x + 110, RX = CIRC.x + CIRC.w - 90;
  const TY = CIRC.y + 80, BY = CIRC.y + CIRC.h - 70;

  function loopPath() {
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(LX, TY);
    ctx.lineTo(RX, TY);
    ctx.lineTo(RX, BY);
    ctx.lineTo(LX, BY);
    ctx.closePath();
  }

  function resistor(cx: number, cy: number) {
    const w = 56, h = 13;
    ctx.fillStyle = bg();
    ctx.fillRect(cx - w / 2 - 2, cy - h - 3, w + 4, 2 * h + 6);
    ctx.strokeStyle = WARM;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2.2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(cx - w / 2, cy);
    for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++)
      ctx.lineTo(cx - w / 2 + (w * (k + 0.5)) / 6, cy + (k % 2 === 0 ? -h : h));
    ctx.lineTo(cx + w / 2, cy);
    ctx.stroke();
  }

  function inductor(cx: number, cy: number) {
    const w = 60, r = 9;
    ctx.fillStyle = bg();
    ctx.fillRect(cx - w / 2 - 2, cy - r - 4, w + 4, r + 10);
    ctx.strokeStyle = ACC;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2.2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(cx - w / 2, cy);
    for (let k = 0; k < 4; k++) {
      const x0 = cx - w / 2 + 6 + k * ((w - 12) / 4);
      ctx.arc(x0 + (w - 12) / 8, cy, (w - 12) / 8, Math.PI, 0, false);
    }
    ctx.lineTo(cx + w / 2, cy);
    ctx.stroke();
  }

  function capacitor(cx: number, cy: number) {
    const gap = 9, plate = 34;
    ctx.fillStyle = bg();
    ctx.fillRect(cx - plate / 2 - 3, cy - gap - 4, plate + 6, 2 * gap + 8);
    ctx.strokeStyle = TEAL;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2.6;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(cx - plate / 2, cy - gap);
    ctx.lineTo(cx + plate / 2, cy - gap);
    ctx.moveTo(cx - plate / 2, cy + gap);
    ctx.lineTo(cx + plate / 2, cy + gap);
    ctx.stroke();
    // the charge actually sitting on the plates
    const n = Math.min(7, Math.round(Math.abs(vC) / (state.amp / 7 || 1)));
    const sign = vC >= 0 ? 1 : -1;
    ctx.fillStyle = TEAL;
    for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) {
      const x = cx - plate / 2 + 5 + (k * (plate - 10)) / Math.max(1, n - 1);
      label(sign > 0 ? '+' : '−', x, cy - gap - 6, 0.9, 'center', 11, TEAL);
      label(sign > 0 ? '−' : '+', x, cy + gap + 15, 0.9, 'center', 11, TEAL);
    }
  }

  function source(cx: number, cy: number, vs: number) {
    ctx.fillStyle = bg();
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(cx, cy, 26, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.55);
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.strokeStyle = WARM;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    if (state.src === 'sine') {
      for (let k = 0; k <= 26; k++) {
        const f = k / 26;
        const x = cx - 14 + f * 28;
        const y = cy - Math.sin(f * Math.PI * 2) * 9;
        k ? ctx.lineTo(x, y) : ctx.moveTo(x, y);
      }
    } else {
      ctx.moveTo(cx - 14, cy + 8);
      ctx.lineTo(cx - 2, cy + 8);
      ctx.lineTo(cx - 2, cy - 8);
      ctx.lineTo(cx + 8, cy - 8);
      if (state.src === 'square') {
        ctx.lineTo(cx + 8, cy + 8);
        ctx.lineTo(cx + 14, cy + 8);
      } else ctx.lineTo(cx + 14, cy - 8);
    }
    ctx.stroke();
    label(`${vs >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${vs.toFixed(2)} V`, cx, cy - 36, 0.95, 'center', 13, WARM);
  }

  let dashPhase = 0;

  function drawCircuit(vs: number) {
    panel(CIRC, 'THE LOOP');
    const midY = (TY + BY) / 2;

    // the wire, with the current drawn as movement along it
    ctx.strokeStyle = Math.abs(i) > 1e-9 ? GREEN : inkA(0.35);
    ctx.lineWidth = 2.4;
    ctx.setLineDash([9, 9]);
    ctx.lineDashOffset = dashPhase;
    loopPath();
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    ctx.lineDashOffset = 0;

    source(LX, midY, vs);

    const rx = LX + (RX - LX) * (hasL() ? 0.33 : 0.5);
    resistor(rx, TY);
    label('R', rx, TY - 26, 0.55, 'center', 12, WARM);
    label(`${(i * state.R).toFixed(2)} V`, rx, TY - 40, 0.95, 'center', 12, WARM);

    if (hasL()) {
      const lx = LX + (RX - LX) * 0.72;
      inductor(lx, TY);
      label('L', lx, TY - 26, 0.55, 'center', 12, ACC);
      const vL = vs - i * state.R - (hasC() ? vC : 0);
      label(`${vL.toFixed(2)} V`, lx, TY - 40, 0.95, 'center', 12, ACC);
    }

    if (hasC()) {
      capacitor(RX, midY);
      label('C', RX + 34, midY - 8, 0.55, 'left', 12, TEAL);
      label(`${vC.toFixed(2)} V`, RX + 34, midY + 10, 0.95, 'left', 12, TEAL);
    }

    // the current, said out loud
    ctx.fillStyle = GREEN;
    ctx.strokeStyle = GREEN;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    const ax = (LX + RX) / 2;
    const dir = Math.sign(i) || 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(ax - dir * 26, BY + 22);
    ctx.lineTo(ax + dir * 26, BY + 22);
    ctx.stroke();
    const a = dir > 0 ? 0 : Math.PI;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(ax + dir * 26, BY + 22);
    ctx.lineTo(ax + dir * 26 - 8 * Math.cos(a - 0.4), BY + 22 - 8 * Math.sin(a - 0.4));
    ctx.lineTo(ax + dir * 26 - 8 * Math.cos(a + 0.4), BY + 22 - 8 * Math.sin(a + 0.4));
    ctx.closePath();
    ctx.fill();
    label(eng(Math.abs(i), 'A'), ax, BY + 44, 0.95, 'center', 12, GREEN);

    label('KVL: v_s = v_R + v_L + v_C', CIRC.x + CIRC.w - 12, CIRC.y + 20, 0.45, 'right', 11);
  }

  // --- energy ----------------------------------------------------------------

  function drawEnergy() {
    panel(ENERGY, 'WHERE THE ENERGY IS');
    const eC = hasC() ? 0.5 * state.C * vC * vC : 0;
    const eL = hasL() ? 0.5 * state.L * i * i : 0;
    const emax = Math.max(1e-12, 0.5 * state.C * state.amp * state.amp * 1.2, eC, eL);
    const px = ENERGY.x + 24, pw = ENERGY.w - 48;

    const bar = (y: number, v: number, col: string, name: string, sub: string) => {
      ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.06);
      rr(px, y, pw, 18, 5);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.fillStyle = col;
      rr(px, y, Math.max(2, (v / emax) * pw), 18, 5);
      ctx.fill();
      label(name, px, y - 7, 0.8, 'left', 11, col);
      label(eng(v, 'J'), px + pw, y - 7, 0.9, 'right', 11, col);
      label(sub, px, y + 32, 0.35, 'left', 10);
    };

    bar(ENERGY.y + 40, eC, TEAL, '½ C v²  in the electric field', 'held as charge pushed apart');
    bar(ENERGY.y + 112, eL, ACC, '½ L i²  in the magnetic field', 'held as current that will not stop');
    bar(ENERGY.y + 190, eDiss, HOT, 'burnt in R since reset', 'gone for good, as heat');

    label(
      state.mode === 'rlc'
        ? 'the two top bars trade back and forth; the bottom one only ever grows'
        : 'one store, so there is nothing to trade with',
      px,
      ENERGY.y + ENERGY.h - 14,
      0.4,
      'left',
      10.5
    );
  }

  // --- the scope -------------------------------------------------------------

  function drawScope() {
    panel(SCOPE, 'VOLTAGES AND CURRENT AGAINST TIME');
    const px = SCOPE.x + 54, py = SCOPE.y + 20, pw = SCOPE.w - 74, ph = SCOPE.h - 60;
    const span = spanOf();
    const t1 = state.src === 'step' ? span : Math.max(span, clock);
    const t0 = t1 - span;
    const X = (t: number) => px + ((t - t0) / span) * pw;

    let vmax = state.amp * 1.15, imax = 1e-9;
    for (const h of hist) {
      vmax = Math.max(vmax, Math.abs(h.vC), Math.abs(h.vL));
      imax = Math.max(imax, Math.abs(h.i));
    }
    const Yv = (v: number) => py + ph * 0.34 - (v / vmax) * (ph * 0.3);
    const Yi = (ii: number) => py + ph * 0.82 - (ii / imax) * (ph * 0.16);

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.18);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    for (const [y, txt] of [
      [Yv(0), '0 V'],
      [Yi(0), '0 A'],
    ] as [number, string][]) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.12);
      ctx.setLineDash([3, 3]);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(px, y);
      ctx.lineTo(px + pw, y);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      label(txt, px - 6, y + 4, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    }
    label(`${vmax.toFixed(1)} V`, px - 6, Yv(vmax) + 4, 0.3, 'right', 9);
    label(eng(imax, 'A', 1), px - 6, Yi(imax) + 4, 0.3, 'right', 9);

    // the 63% mark, and where one time constant lands
    if (state.src !== 'sine' && state.mode !== 'rlc') {
      const y = Yv(state.amp * 0.632);
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.3);
      ctx.setLineDash([2, 4]);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(px, y);
      ctx.lineTo(px + pw, y);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      label('63%', px + pw - 2, y - 5, 0.5, 'right', 10);
      // one τ after the rising edge, which for a step is the start of time
      const edge = state.src === 'step' ? 0 : (hist.find((h) => h.vs > state.amp * 0.5)?.t ?? NaN);
      if (Number.isFinite(edge) && edge + tauOf() < t1 && edge + tauOf() > t0) {
        const xt = X(edge + tauOf());
        ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.3);
        ctx.setLineDash([2, 4]);
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(xt, py);
        ctx.lineTo(xt, py + ph);
        ctx.stroke();
        ctx.setLineDash([]);
        label('one τ', xt + 4, py + 14, 0.5, 'left', 10);
      }
    }

    if (hist.length > 1) {
      const series: [string, (h: Sample) => number, number, boolean][] = [
        [WARM, (h) => Yv(h.vs), 1.8, true],
        [TEAL, (h) => Yv(h.vC), 2.4, hasC()],
        [ACC, (h) => Yv(h.vL), 1.8, hasL()],
        [GREEN, (h) => Yi(h.i), 2, true],
      ];
      for (const [col, fn, lw, on] of series) {
        if (!on) continue;
        ctx.strokeStyle = col;
        ctx.lineWidth = lw;
        ctx.beginPath();
        hist.forEach((h, k) => (k ? ctx.lineTo(X(h.t), fn(h)) : ctx.moveTo(X(h.t), fn(h))));
        ctx.stroke();
      }
    }
    let lx = px + 6;
    const legend: [string, string, boolean][] = [
      [WARM, 'source', true],
      [TEAL, 'v_C', hasC()],
      [ACC, 'v_L', hasL()],
      [GREEN, 'current', true],
    ];
    for (const [c, t, on] of legend) {
      if (!on) continue;
      label(t, lx, py + 12, 0.85, 'left', 10.5, c);
      lx += 58;
    }
    label(`${eng(span, 's', 1)} across`, px + pw, py + ph + 18, 0.4, 'right', 10);
  }

  // --- the poles -------------------------------------------------------------

  function poles(): { re: number; im: number }[] {
    if (state.mode === 'rc') return [{ re: -1 / (state.R * state.C), im: 0 }];
    if (state.mode === 'rl') return [{ re: -state.R / state.L, im: 0 }];
    const z = zeta(), w = w0();
    if (z < 1) return [
      { re: -z * w, im: w * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z) },
      { re: -z * w, im: -w * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z) },
    ];
    const d = w * Math.sqrt(z * z - 1);
    return [{ re: -z * w + d, im: 0 }, { re: -z * w - d, im: 0 }];
  }

  function drawPoles() {
    panel(POLES, 'WHERE THE POLES SIT');
    const px = POLES.x + 20, py = POLES.y + 22, pw = POLES.w - 40, ph = POLES.h - 70;
    const ps = poles();
    const scale = Math.max(...ps.map((p) => Math.hypot(p.re, p.im)), w0()) * 1.35;
    const ox = px + pw * 0.78, oy = py + ph / 2;
    const X = (re: number) => ox + (re / scale) * pw * 0.72;
    const Y = (im: number) => oy - (im / scale) * (ph / 2) * 0.86;

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.18);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, oy);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, oy);
    ctx.moveTo(ox, py);
    ctx.lineTo(ox, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    label('σ', px + pw - 2, oy + 14, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    label('jω', ox + 6, py + 8, 0.35, 'left', 10);

    // the circle of constant ω₀: the poles slide along it as R changes
    if (state.mode === 'rlc' && zeta() < 1) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.14);
      ctx.setLineDash([3, 4]);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(ox, oy, (w0() / scale) * pw * 0.72, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      label('ω₀', ox - (w0() / scale) * pw * 0.72 - 6, oy - 8, 0.4, 'right', 10);
    }

    // anything to the right of the axis would grow instead of decay
    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(249,115,106,0.06)';
    ctx.fillRect(ox, py, px + pw - ox, ph);
    label('unstable', px + pw - 4, py + ph - 4, 0.3, 'right', 9, HOT);

    for (const p of ps) {
      const x = X(p.re), y = Y(p.im);
      ctx.strokeStyle = zeta() < 1 && state.mode === 'rlc' ? TEAL : ACC;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2.4;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(x - 7, y - 7);
      ctx.lineTo(x + 7, y + 7);
      ctx.moveTo(x + 7, y - 7);
      ctx.lineTo(x - 7, y + 7);
      ctx.stroke();
    }

    const z = zeta();
    const regime =
      state.mode !== 'rlc'
        ? 'one real pole: a plain exponential'
        : z < 0.98
          ? 'underdamped: a complex pair, so it rings'
          : z < 1.02
            ? 'critically damped: as fast as it gets without overshoot'
            : 'overdamped: two real poles, sluggish';
    label(regime, px, POLES.y + POLES.h - 30, 0.7, 'left', 11, z < 0.98 && state.mode === 'rlc' ? TEAL : ACC);
    label(
      'the real part sets how fast it dies, the imaginary part how fast it rings',
      px,
      POLES.y + POLES.h - 12,
      0.35,
      'left',
      10
    );
  }

  // --- frequency response ----------------------------------------------------

  /** |output / source|, with the output being whatever the scope highlights. */
  function mag(f: number) {
    const w = 2 * Math.PI * f;
    if (state.mode === 'rc') return 1 / Math.hypot(1, w * state.R * state.C);
    if (state.mode === 'rl') return 1 / Math.hypot(1, (w * state.L) / state.R);
    const wr = w / w0();
    return 1 / Math.hypot(1 - wr * wr, 2 * zeta() * wr);
  }

  function drawBode() {
    panel(BODE, state.mode === 'rl' ? 'CURRENT THROUGH, BY FREQUENCY' : 'WHAT REACHES THE CAPACITOR, BY FREQUENCY');
    const px = BODE.x + 50, py = BODE.y + 22, pw = BODE.w - 68, ph = BODE.h - 62;
    const f0 = fchar();
    const lo = Math.log10(f0 / 100), hi = Math.log10(f0 * 100);
    const X = (f: number) => px + ((Math.log10(f) - lo) / (hi - lo)) * pw;
    const DBMAX = 26, DBMIN = -62;
    const Y = (db: number) => py + ph - ((Math.max(DBMIN, Math.min(DBMAX, db)) - DBMIN) / (DBMAX - DBMIN)) * ph;

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.18);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    for (const db of [20, 0, -20, -40, -60]) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(db === 0 ? 0.22 : 0.08);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(px, Y(db));
      ctx.lineTo(px + pw, Y(db));
      ctx.stroke();
      label(`${db} dB`, px - 6, Y(db) + 4, 0.35, 'right', 9.5);
    }
    let tick = 0;
    for (let d = Math.ceil(lo); d <= hi; d++) {
      const f = 10 ** d;
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.08);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(X(f), py);
      ctx.lineTo(X(f), py + ph);
      ctx.stroke();
      if (tick++ % 2 === 0) label(eng(f, 'Hz', 0), X(f), py + ph + 16, 0.3, 'center', 9.5);
    }

    ctx.strokeStyle = TEAL;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2.2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let k = 0; k <= 240; k++) {
      const f = 10 ** (lo + ((hi - lo) * k) / 240);
      const y = Y(20 * Math.log10(mag(f)));
      k ? ctx.lineTo(X(f), y) : ctx.moveTo(X(f), y);
    }
    ctx.stroke();

    // the corner, which is the same number the step response showed
    ctx.strokeStyle = ACC;
    ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(X(f0), py);
    ctx.lineTo(X(f0), py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    label(
      state.mode === 'rlc' ? `f₀ = ${eng(f0, 'Hz', 1)}` : `1/2πτ = ${eng(f0, 'Hz', 1)}`,
      X(f0) + 5,
      py + 14,
      0.8,
      'left',
      11,
      ACC
    );

    if (state.src === 'sine') {
      const f = driveF();
      const fc = Math.max(10 ** lo, Math.min(10 ** hi, f));
      const y = Y(20 * Math.log10(mag(f)));
      ctx.fillStyle = WARM;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(X(fc), y, 5.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      label(
        `gain ${mag(f).toFixed(2)}×`,
        Math.min(X(fc) + 9, px + pw - 4),
        y - 9,
        0.95,
        X(fc) > px + pw - 80 ? 'right' : 'left',
        11,
        WARM
      );
    } else {
      label('a sine source puts its dot here', px + pw, py + 14, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    }
  }

  // --- readouts --------------------------------------------------------------

  const el = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const setRow = (n: number, lab: string, val: string) => {
    el('l' + n).innerHTML = subHtml(lab);
    el('r' + n).textContent = val;
  };
  function updateReadout() {
    const vs = vSource(clock);
    setRow(1, 'Source', vs.toFixed(2) + ' V');
    setRow(2, 'Current', eng(i, 'A'));
    setRow(3, hasC() ? 'Capacitor v_C' : 'Inductor v_L', (hasC() ? vC : vs - i * state.R).toFixed(2) + ' V');
    setRow(4, 'Time constant τ', eng(tauOf(), 's'));
    if (state.mode === 'rlc') {
      setRow(5, 'Natural f_0', eng(fchar(), 'Hz'));
      setRow(6, 'Damping ζ', zeta().toFixed(3));
      setRow(7, 'Quality Q', (1 / (2 * zeta())).toFixed(2));
    } else {
      setRow(5, 'Corner frequency', eng(fchar(), 'Hz'));
      setRow(6, 'Damping ζ', '—');
      setRow(7, 'Quality Q', '—');
    }
    setRow(8, 'Heat burnt in R', eng(eDiss, 'J'));
  }

  // --- frame -----------------------------------------------------------------

  function draw() {
    const vs = vSource(clock);
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    label(
      state.mode === 'rc' ? 'RC' : state.mode === 'rl' ? 'RL' : 'RLC',
      20,
      30,
      0.85,
      'left',
      14
    );
    drawCircuit(vs);
    if (state.aux === 'poles') drawPoles();
    else if (state.aux === 'bode') drawBode();
    else drawEnergy();
    drawScope();
  }

  let last = performance.now();
  function frame(now: number) {
    let dt = (now - last) / 1000;
    last = now;
    dt = Math.min(0.05, Math.max(0, dt));
    if (state.running) {
      physics(dt);
      // the dashes move at a speed you can read, not at the circuit's own
      const iFull = state.amp / state.R || 1;
      dashPhase -= Math.sign(i) * Math.min(140, (Math.abs(i) / iFull) * 70) * dt;
    }
    draw();
    updateReadout();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  // --- controls --------------------------------------------------------------

  const runBtn = el('run');
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.running = !state.running;
    runBtn.textContent = state.running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
  });
  el('reset').addEventListener('click', reset);

  let ready = false;
  function bindRange(id: string, apply: (n: number) => void, restart = false) {
    const input = document.getElementById(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    const run = () => {
      apply(+input.value);
      if (restart && ready) reset();
    };
    input.addEventListener('input', run);
    run();
  }
  bindRange('amp', (n) => {
    state.amp = n / 10;
    el('ampval').textContent = `${state.amp.toFixed(1)} V`;
  });
  bindRange('freq', (n) => {
    state.fmul = 10 ** (n / 100);
    syncFreqLabel();
  });
  bindRange('r', (n) => {
    state.R = Math.round(10 ** (1 + n / 100));
    el('rval').textContent = `${state.R} Ω`;
    syncFreqLabel();
  }, true);
  bindRange('l', (n) => {
    state.L = n / 1000;
    el('lval').textContent = eng(state.L, 'H');
    syncFreqLabel();
  }, true);
  bindRange('c', (n) => {
    state.C = n * 1e-7;
    el('cval').textContent = eng(state.C, 'F');
    syncFreqLabel();
  }, true);
  bindRange('rate', (n) => {
    state.rate = n / 100;
    el('rateval').textContent = `${state.rate.toFixed(1)}×`;
  });

  function syncFreqLabel() {
    el('fval').textContent = `${state.fmul.toFixed(2)}× (${eng(driveF(), 'Hz', 1)})`;
  }

  function syncMode() {
    el('ctl-l').style.display = hasL() ? '' : 'none';
    el('ctl-c').style.display = hasC() ? '' : 'none';
    el('ctl-f').style.display = state.src === 'step' ? 'none' : '';
    syncFreqLabel();
  }

  function setAux(a: 'energy' | 'poles' | 'bode') {
    state.aux = a;
    document.querySelectorAll('#aux button').forEach((b) => {
      b.classList.toggle('active', (b as HTMLElement).dataset.a === a);
    });
  }
  el('aux').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    setAux(btn.dataset.a as 'energy' | 'poles' | 'bode');
  });

  el('mode').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#mode button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.mode = btn.dataset.m as Mode;
    syncMode();
    reset();
  });
  el('src').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#src button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.src = btn.dataset.s as Src;
    // a sine drive is the frequency-response experiment, so show Bode
    if (state.src === 'sine') setAux('bode');
    syncMode();
    reset();
  });

  syncMode();
  reset();
  ready = true;
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
</script>

<style>
  #rlc {
    touch-action: none;
  }
  .scale-hint {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin-top: 3px;
  }
</style>
